            "navTitle": "Chapter 3: Understanding Data Fundamentals",
            "content": "# Chapter 3: Understanding Data Fundamentals\n\nBusiness decisions depend on data, but organizations do not gain value just by collecting more of it. They gain value when recorded values are defined clearly, stored consistently, and interpreted in the right context. Serving as the bridge from general information systems to structured tables, this chapter explores what data actually is and how it transforms from raw values into meaningful insight. By the end, you will understand why a trustworthy data foundation is essential before any database tool or SQL query enters the picture.\n\nIn Chapter 2, you learned why information systems matter to organizational performance. This chapter narrows the focus from the system to the data itself. The practical question is simple: what kinds of data do organizations have, how should that data be represented, and what makes it usable, trustworthy, and ready for databases and analysis?\n\n## Chapter Video\n\n<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/dDJM0lB2654\" title=\"Chapter 3 overview video\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n\n[Watch the Chapter 3 overview video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDJM0lB2654)\n\n# Chapter Roadmap\n\n| Topic | Why It Matters |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Why Data Fundamentals Drive Business Performance](#why-data-fundamentals-drive-business-performance) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Data, Meaning, and Context](#data-meaning-and-context) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Classifying Data](#classifying-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Qualitative versus quantitative data](#qualitative-versus-quantitative-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Categorical versus numerical data](#categorical-versus-numerical-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Representing Data in Structured Systems](#representing-data-in-structured-systems) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Tables: Rows, Columns, and Rules](#tables-rows-columns-and-rules) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Schemas: Describing the Structure of Data](#schemas-describing-the-structure-of-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [From Spreadsheets to Databases](#from-spreadsheets-to-databases) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Managing Data as an Organizational Asset](#managing-data-as-an-organizational-asset) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n\n---",
