            "title": "Answer Key",
            "navTitle": "Answer Key",
            "content": "# Answer Key\n\n1. A strong answer defines the first half as one connected framework, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n2. A strong answer defines data and information, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n3. A strong answer defines databases and dbms concepts, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n4. A strong answer defines tables, keys, and relationships, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n5. A strong answer defines sql and query logic, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n6. A strong answer defines normalization and data quality, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n7. A strong answer defines why this review matters, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n8. A strong answer defines what to review before the midterm, explains why it matters, and connects it to trustworthy data work or business performance.\n\n9. Strong responses connect one chapter idea to a concrete course project decision.\n\n10. Strong responses identify a specific uncertainty and explain what evidence or practice would resolve it.",
