            "navTitle": "Readiness Assessment Test (RAT): Chapter 8 - Midterm Review…",
            "content": "# Readiness Assessment Test (RAT): Chapter 8 - Midterm Review — Concepts\n\nComplete this assessment after reading the chapter and before class.\n\n**1. Which statement best describes the first half as one connected framework in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**2. Which statement best describes data and information in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**3. Which statement best describes databases and dbms concepts in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**4. Which statement best describes tables, keys, and relationships in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**5. Which statement best describes sql and query logic in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**6. Which statement best describes normalization and data quality in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**7. Which statement best describes why this review matters in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**8. Which statement best describes what to review before the midterm in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**9. Which statement best describes midterm test instructions in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**10. Which statement best describes files for the midterm test in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.",
