            "navTitle": "Chapter 12: Business Intelligence and Analytics for…",
            "content": "# Chapter 12: Business Intelligence and Analytics for Performance Improvement\n\nBusiness Intelligence, or BI, is where the database becomes useful to managers. Earlier chapters focused on how data is structured, queried, designed, and administered. This chapter shifts to the question that motivates all of that work: how do organizations use reliable data to understand performance and make better decisions? It introduces operational versus analytical systems, data warehouses, ETL and ELT pipelines, dimensional modeling, star schemas, OLAP operations, dashboards, KPIs, governance, and the Balanced Scorecard, using the Grading Database as the running example.\n\n## Chapter Video\n\n> **Video placeholder:** Chapter 12 overview video will be added here before publication.\n\n# Chapter Roadmap\n\n| Topic | Why It Matters |\n| --- | --- |\n| [12.1 Business Intelligence Fundamentals](#12-1-business-intelligence-fundamentals) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [What Is Business Intelligence?](#what-is-business-intelligence) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [BI as Decision Support](#bi-as-decision-support) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [BI and the DIKW Hierarchy](#bi-and-the-dikw-hierarchy) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [BI and the R.E.A.D. Framework](#bi-and-the-r-e-a-d-framework) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [12.2 Operational Systems vs. Analytical Systems](#12-2-operational-systems-vs-analytical-systems) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [OLTP: Systems That Run the Business](#oltp-systems-that-run-the-business) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [OLAP: Systems That Analyze the Business](#olap-systems-that-analyze-the-business) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [OLTP vs. OLAP](#oltp-vs-olap) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Why Not Just Analyze the Operational Database?](#why-not-just-analyze-the-operational-database) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n\n---",
