    "navTitle": "Chapter 5: SQL — The Language of Databases",
    "content": "# Chapter 5: SQL — The Language of Databases\n\nChapter 4 introduced databases as structured systems for storing, protecting, and managing data. Chapter 5 introduces the language used to work with those systems: **SQL**, or **Structured Query Language**.\n\nSQL is the standard language used to define database structures, insert records, retrieve results, and summarize patterns. It is one of the most transferable skills in business technology because the same core logic appears across Microsoft Access, SQLite, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Oracle, and cloud data platforms. Later chapters extend SQL into reusable patterns and safe data modification.\n\n## Chapter Video\n\n<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/-QBMQXInrAg\" title=\"Chapter 5 overview video\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n\n[Watch the Chapter 5 overview video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-QBMQXInrAg)\n\n# Chapter Roadmap\n\n| Topic | Why It Matters |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Part 1: SQL Foundations and Tools](#part-1-sql-foundations-and-tools) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Part 2: The Chapter 5 Teaching Dataset](#part-2-the-chapter-5-teaching-dataset) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Part 3: Creating Tables and Inserting Data](#part-3-creating-tables-and-inserting-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Part 4: Querying Data with SELECT](#part-4-querying-data-with-select) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Part 5: A First Look at Joins](#part-5-a-first-look-at-joins) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Part 6: Aggregation, Grouping, and Calculated Results](#part-6-aggregation-grouping-and-calculated-results) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Looking Ahead](#looking-ahead) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Appendix: Applying These Concepts to the Grading Database](#appendix-applying-these-concepts-to-the-grading-database) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Chapter Summary](#chapter-summary) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n\n---",
