    "title": "Chapter 9: Database Design and ER Modeling",
    "navTitle": "Chapter 9: Database Design and ER Modeling",
    "content": "# Chapter 9: Database Design and ER Modeling\n\n*Figure 9.1 — The database design lifecycle translates business requirements into physical tables.*\n\nUp to this point, we have built database objects, worked with tables, created relationships, normalized data, and written SQL queries to retrieve and analyze information. That sequence matters because it gave us practical experience with what databases can do. But there is an important shift we need to make now.\n\n## Chapter Video\n\n<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Q0LRaJ1wl_I\" title=\"Chapter 9 overview video\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n\n[Watch the Chapter 9 overview video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q0LRaJ1wl_I)\n\n# Chapter Roadmap\n\n| Topic | Why It Matters |\n| --- | --- |\n| [9.1 From Querying Data to Designing Systems](#9-1-from-querying-data-to-designing-systems) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.2 The Cost of Poor Design: Data Anomalies](#9-2-the-cost-of-poor-design-data-anomalies) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.3 Database Design in the System Development Life Cycle](#9-3-database-design-in-the-system-development-life-cycle) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.4 From Requirements to Structure](#9-4-from-requirements-to-structure) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.5 Entity-Relationship Modeling](#9-5-entity-relationship-modeling) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.6 Crow's Foot Notation](#9-6-crow-s-foot-notation) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.7 Understanding Relationship Types](#9-7-understanding-relationship-types) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.8 Advanced ER Modeling Concepts](#9-8-advanced-er-modeling-concepts) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.9 Normalization as a Design-Quality Check](#9-9-normalization-as-a-design-quality-check) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [9.10 From ER Diagrams to Relational Tables](#9-10-from-er-diagrams-to-relational-tables) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n\n---",
