    "content": "# Chapter 14: Power BI — Data Visualization and Business Reporting\n\nThis chapter introduces Microsoft Power BI as the industry-standard tool for turning database output into visual business reports. The chapter covers connecting data sources, building data models, creating calculated columns and measures (DAX), designing interactive dashboards, and presenting findings to a non-technical audience. The chapter ties directly to SQL output and the Grading Database as the source data.\n\n- Connect Power BI to a database source and build a basic data model - Create interactive visuals and dashboards that answer a defined business question - Design a report layout appropriate for a managerial audience\n\n## Chapter Video\n\n> **Video placeholder:** Chapter 14 overview video will be added here before publication.\n\n# Chapter Roadmap\n\n| Topic | Why It Matters |\n| --- | --- |\n| [14.2 Connecting to Data Sources](#14-2-connecting-to-data-sources) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [14.3 Power Query: Transforming Data](#14-3-power-query-transforming-data) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [14.4 Building Visualizations](#14-4-building-visualizations) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [14.5 DAX: Data Analysis Expressions](#14-5-dax-data-analysis-expressions) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [14.6 Interactive Reports: Slicers and Filters](#14-6-interactive-reports-slicers-and-filters) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [14.7 Publishing and Sharing](#14-7-publishing-and-sharing) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Chapter Summary](#chapter-summary) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Key Terms](#key-terms) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Review Questions](#review-questions) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n| [Create a semantic model](#create-a-semantic-model) | Key topic in this chapter's Core Concepts reading. |\n\n---",
