    "content": "# Readiness Assessment Test (RAT): Chapter 17 - Designing Systems That Matter\n\nComplete this assessment after reading the chapter and before class.\n\n**1. Which statement best describes chapter 17: designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**2. Which statement best describes conclusion: designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**3. Which statement best describes course integration in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**4. Which statement best describes professional practice in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**5. Which statement best describes continuing development in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**6. Which statement best describes final reflection in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**7. Which statement best describes designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**8. Which statement best describes designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**9. Which statement best describes designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.\n\n**10. Which statement best describes designing systems that matter in this chapter?**\n\nA. It is unrelated to database or information-systems work.\n\nB. It is a chapter concept that supports more reliable data, analysis, or business decisions.\n\nC. It replaces the need for keys, queries, or documentation.\n\nD. It matters only after the course is complete.",
